(3046357, 426111, 48524, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club...<br/> <br/>Having just started to experiment with black and white nudes myself, I realize what a difficult task it is to light well and present a tasteful image.  I think you did a great job in both areas; I would watch the highlights on her skin a litle more on the left breast and going up to her shoulder, though.  A tiny bit of burning might help to take that down a little bit.<br/> <br/>Though having her centered and practically filling the frame makes her seem like a much more important figure (as indicated in your title, we can assume she''s important to you :) ) I almost feel like the way she''s lit would seem more effective if you had left more negative space, maybe just to the darker side of her body so that she is less centered and seems to have a longer ''shadow''.<br/> <br/>Great processing on the skin, and for the tones overall.  The necklace is an especially nice touch.  Very beautiful model, and an overall great shot.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me with any questions.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club... Having just started to experiment with black and white nudes myself, I realize what a difficult task it is to light well and present a tasteful image.  I think you did a great job in both areas; I would watch the highlights on her skin a litle more on the left breast and going up to her shoulder, though.  A tiny bit of burning might help to take that down a little bit. Though having her centered and practically filling the frame makes her seem like a much more important figure (as indicated in your title, we can assume she''s important to you :) ) I almost feel like the way she''s lit would seem more effective if you had left more negative space, maybe just to the darker side of her body so that she is less centered and seems to have a longer ''shadow''. Great processing on the skin, and for the tones overall.  The necklace is an especially nice touch.  Very beautiful model, and an overall great shot. Feel free to PM me with any questions.', '2006-11-20 05:51:55.000000', NULL, 0),
