(3047198, 426482, 67841, '<td valign="top">Beautiful subject &amp; nice framing, but watch out with this lense!  Considering the old Pentax SMCA 1.4 was one of the sharpest 50mm lenses of its day (giving Zeiss &amp; Leica a run for their money) it would be a shame if you found yourself with soft shots all the time because of tight DOF. Try stopping down a bit to get better performance out of the ol'' 50mm - it took me awhile to learn that but mostly because I love the gobs of great bokeh this lense produces.  At f1.4 (wide open), this lens'' DOF is measured in fractions of an inch - but there are plenty of times I LOVE that much soft focus so don''t take my advice as a rule. FYI, I find that somewhere between f5.6 &amp; f8 are the stops I use when I''m concerned about keeping things in focus.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-11-20 10:46:20.</i></td>', 'Beautiful subject & nice framing, but watch out with this lense!  Considering the old Pentax SMCA 1.4 was one of the sharpest 50mm lenses of its day (giving Zeiss & Leica a run for their money) it would be a shame if you found yourself with soft shots all the time because of tight DOF. Try stopping down a bit to get better performance out of the ol'' 50mm - it took me awhile to learn that but mostly because I love the gobs of great bokeh this lense produces.  At f1.4 (wide open), this lens'' DOF is measured in fractions of an inch - but there are plenty of times I LOVE that much soft focus so don''t take my advice as a rule. FYI, I find that somewhere between f5.6 & f8 are the stops I use when I''m concerned about keeping things in focus.', '2006-11-20 10:45:15.000000', '2006-11-20 10:46:20.000000', 0),
(3047260, 424104, 16046, '<td valign="top">Nice composition, skyscrapers all in line down to the Smith tower, great point of view. well done.</td>', 'Nice composition, skyscrapers all in line down to the Smith tower, great point of view. well done.', '2006-11-20 11:05:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(3047277, 426090, 52549, '<td valign="top">WTG Richard, Crystal clear shot, great b/w.</td>', 'WTG Richard, Crystal clear shot, great b/w.', '2006-11-20 11:10:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(3047281, 426762, 57229, '<td valign="top">Definitely agree with the symbolic heft. Less sure about the specific interpretation or tale attached, but yes, the picture screams out to have its story told even though it doesn''t tell us exactly what the story is.<br/> <br/>One sure quality that this picture has, which I thought around half of the entries lacked, is that it is immensely better for being in black and white. Colour would subtract/distract from both the emotive human content and the geometric symbols of the sailors'' suits.<br/> <br/>Pleased to see it.</td>', 'Definitely agree with the symbolic heft. Less sure about the specific interpretation or tale attached, but yes, the picture screams out to have its story told even though it doesn''t tell us exactly what the story is. One sure quality that this picture has, which I thought around half of the entries lacked, is that it is immensely better for being in black and white. Colour would subtract/distract from both the emotive human content and the geometric symbols of the sailors'' suits. Pleased to see it.', '2006-11-20 11:13:20.000000', NULL, 0),
