(3047420, 426759, 7778, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> Finding some way to snip off and perfect some distortion of the Universe, that is the essence of photography. This is the essence of photography. The running child keeps this from being too cold. It''s all just part of the fine-tuning of this perfection. 10 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well, I wouldn''t call it ''perfect'' or give it a 10 (coz I feel light and tonalities can be improved upon), but, otherwise, posthumous has it perfectly right: this is a photographer''s photo, a classic (something that just won''t go stale), really, with a <i>poise</i> of a composition.<br/> <br/>A remarkable shot, exemplary and fit for study.</td>', 'Originally posted by posthumous: Finding some way to snip off and perfect some distortion of the Universe, that is the essence of photography. This is the essence of photography. The running child keeps this from being too cold. It''s all just part of the fine-tuning of this perfection. 10   Well, I wouldn''t call it ''perfect'' or give it a 10 (coz I feel light and tonalities can be improved upon), but, otherwise, posthumous has it perfectly right: this is a photographer''s photo, a classic (something that just won''t go stale), really, with a poise of a composition. A remarkable shot, exemplary and fit for study.', '2006-11-20 11:52:44.000000', NULL, 0),
