(3048794, 425795, 2382, '<td valign="top">thanks for the feedback folks!  I realized that my pet shot was probably not going to be very well scored but just had to take it anyway.  My poodle is a "Blue Standard" and now at 11yrs old is pretty much black and white so i thought i would give a try to capture a portrait.  I''ve got tons of snapshots of her and she is very UN photogenic.  Usually her eyes aren''t visible so, i put a small spot behind me to reflect.  this is probably the best picture i have of her since i took a little bit of time to think about it.  With the tips rec''d here now it''s time to go back and improve on it.  Don''t worry, i porbably won''t enter a challenge with her again.... unless i just can''t help myself.<br/> <br/>thanks for the replies!<br/> <br/>carlos</td>', 'thanks for the feedback folks!  I realized that my pet shot was probably not going to be very well scored but just had to take it anyway.  My poodle is a "Blue Standard" and now at 11yrs old is pretty much black and white so i thought i would give a try to capture a portrait.  I''ve got tons of snapshots of her and she is very UN photogenic.  Usually her eyes aren''t visible so, i put a small spot behind me to reflect.  this is probably the best picture i have of her since i took a little bit of time to think about it.  With the tips rec''d here now it''s time to go back and improve on it.  Don''t worry, i porbably won''t enter a challenge with her again.... unless i just can''t help myself. thanks for the replies! carlos', '2006-11-20 18:49:05.000000', NULL, 0),
