(3049693, 425922, 42013, '<td valign="top">HI from the Critique Club...<br/> <br/>Hope this critique can give you a couple of things to think about. If you have any questions just pm me.<br/> <br/>My first impression is WOW! This is a striking photo. It is a little disconcerting with the CW rotation but it makes for an interesting portrait in a sea of more standard ones.<br/> <br/>Its very free form and fun, so in that spirit, the arm accross half of her face really doesn''t bother me. I do wish there were a little more darkness on the upper half of the pic to balance out the lower half.<br/> <br/>When i twist my head around to view the ''right'' way, it still presents itself a strong portrait and one that communicates a lot of joy. IN short, its technically strong, it''s fun, and it meets the challenge. It may not be the strongest BW subject as its impact is more muted but a wonderful image and one you and she should be proud of.<br/> <br/>Good luck in future challenges.</td>', 'HI from the Critique Club... Hope this critique can give you a couple of things to think about. If you have any questions just pm me. My first impression is WOW! This is a striking photo. It is a little disconcerting with the CW rotation but it makes for an interesting portrait in a sea of more standard ones. Its very free form and fun, so in that spirit, the arm accross half of her face really doesn''t bother me. I do wish there were a little more darkness on the upper half of the pic to balance out the lower half. When i twist my head around to view the ''right'' way, it still presents itself a strong portrait and one that communicates a lot of joy. IN short, its technically strong, it''s fun, and it meets the challenge. It may not be the strongest BW subject as its impact is more muted but a wonderful image and one you and she should be proud of. Good luck in future challenges.', '2006-11-21 01:43:56.000000', NULL, 0),
